---
// /developers/: docs for the free public API (/api/v1/*) and the remote MCP server (/mcp). English-only (like /guides/):
// hreflang en + x-default, listed once in sitemap-en.xml. /api redirects here (functions/api/index.js).
// No affiliate links on this page: examples use non-partner tools. The API/MCP output labels affiliate links (affiliate, disclosure).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
import { publicTools, publicCategories, FILTERS, RATE_LIMITS, MCP_URL } from "../lib/publicApi";
import { TOOLS as MCP_TOOLS, SUPPORTED as MCP_VERSIONS } from "../../functions/_lib/mcp.js";
const url = `${SITE.url}/developers/`;
const title = "Free API & MCP server";
const desc = `Free, read-only JSON API and remote MCP server for the TradingAIHub directory of ${publicTools.length} AI tools for finance and trading. No sign-in, no key, CORS enabled.`;
const ld = [
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebAPI", name: "TradingAIHub public API", description: desc, url, documentation: url,
    termsOfService: `${SITE.url}/terms/`, provider: { "@id": `${SITE.url}/#organization` }, isAccessibleForFree: true },
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [
    { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE.url}/` },
    { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: title, item: url } ] },
];
const ex = publicTools.find((t) => t.slug === "alpha-vantage-mcp") ?? publicTools[0];
const sample = JSON.stringify({ tool: { slug: ex.slug, name: ex.name, type: ex.type, category: ex.category, description: ex.description, url: ex.url, website_url: ex.website_url, vendor_url: ex.vendor_url, affiliate: ex.affiliate, disclosure: ex.disclosure, homepage: ex.homepage, remote_mcp_url: ex.remote_mcp_url, license: ex.license, pricing: ex.pricing ? { model: ex.pricing.model, free_tier: ex.pricing.free_tier } : null, languages: ex.languages, status: ex.status, verified: ex.verified, checked_at: ex.checked_at, "…": "…" } }, null, 2);
const B = SITE.url;
const curl = `# Every verified market-data MCP server
curl -s "${B}/api/v1/tools?category=market-data&type=mcp&verified=true"

# One tool
curl -s "${B}/api/v1/tools/${ex.slug}"

# Search
curl -s "${B}/api/v1/search?q=options+data&limit=5"

# Categories, and the full dump
curl -s "${B}/api/v1/categories"
curl -sO "${B}/api/v1/tools.json"`;
const js = `const res = await fetch("${B}/api/v1/search?q=" + encodeURIComponent("crypto exchange"));
if (!res.ok) throw new Error((await res.json()).error.message);
const { tools } = await res.json();
for (const t of tools) console.log(t.name, t.status, t.url);`;
const py = `import requests

r = requests.get("${B}/api/v1/tools",
                 params={"category": "trading-brokers", "verified": "true", "limit": 20},
                 timeout=10)
r.raise_for_status()
for t in r.json()["tools"]:
    print(t["name"], "-", t["remote_mcp_url"] or t["homepage"])`;
const prompt = `You can look up AI tools for finance and trading in the free TradingAIHub API (no key).
- Search: GET ${B}/api/v1/search?q=<keywords>
- Details: GET ${B}/api/v1/tools/<slug>
- Filters: GET ${B}/api/v1/tools?category=<slug>&type=mcp|skill|api&verified=true
- Spec: ${B}/api/openapi.json
Prefer tools with "verified": true, cite each tool's "url", and say that this is not investment advice.`;
const claudeDesktop = JSON.stringify({ mcpServers: { tradingaihub: { command: "npx", args: ["-y", "mcp-remote", MCP_URL] } } }, null, 2);
const cursor = JSON.stringify({ mcpServers: { tradingaihub: { url: MCP_URL } } }, null, 2);
const vscode = JSON.stringify({ servers: { tradingaihub: { type: "http", url: MCP_URL } } }, null, 2);
const rpc = `curl -s ${MCP_URL} \\
  -H "content-type: application/json" -H "accept: application/json, text/event-stream" \\
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"search_tools","arguments":{"query":"stock prices","limit":3}}}'`;
const endpoints = [
  ["/api/v1/tools", "List tools. Filters: category, type, language, status, verified, official; limit (1–100, default 50), offset. Sorted by name, with total and a next link."],
  ["/api/v1/tools/{slug}", "One tool. Unknown slug → 404 JSON."],
  ["/api/v1/search?q=", "Search name, description, category and package names. Tools matching every word rank first, then partial matches. Optional category, type, limit (1–50, default 10)."],
  ["/api/v1/categories", `All ${publicCategories.length} categories with tool counts.`],
  ["/api/v1/tools.json", "Full dump of every tool (same objects as /api/v1/tools)."],
  ["/api/v1/categories.json", "Same as /api/v1/categories, as a file."],
  ["/api/openapi.json", "OpenAPI 3.1 description of all of the above."],
];
---
<Base title={title} description={desc} jsonld={ld} lang="en" langs={["en"]}>
<div class="wrap page prose">
  <div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / {title}</div>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <p>{desc} The data is the same as on the site: every MCP server, agent skill and API we list, with pricing, license, published packages and the result of our weekly verification. These docs are in English.</p>
  <p class="callout">Information only, not investment advice. Affiliate disclosure: for partner tools (currently TradingView and EODHD), <code>website_url</code> is the same affiliate link the site uses, marked <code>affiliate: true</code> with a <code>disclosure</code>; <code>vendor_url</code> is always the plain link. TradingAIHub may earn a commission, and listings never depend on payment. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>, <a href="/terms/">terms</a> and <a href="/about/">how we verify</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="rest">REST API</h2>
  <p>Base URL <code>{B}</code>. Only <code>GET</code> (and <code>HEAD</code>, <code>OPTIONS</code>); anything else returns 405. Every response is JSON with <code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *</code>, so you can call it from a browser. Successful responses are cacheable (<code>Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600</code>). The full spec is at <a href="/api/openapi.json">/api/openapi.json</a>.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>What it returns</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {endpoints.map(([p, d]) => <tr><td><code>{p}</code></td><td>{d}</td></tr>)}
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h3>Filter values</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><code>category</code>: {FILTERS.category.map((c, i) => <>{i ? ", " : ""}<code>{c}</code></>)}</li>
    <li><code>type</code>: <code>mcp</code>, <code>skill</code>, <code>api</code></li>
    <li><code>status</code>: the weekly check result: {FILTERS.status.map((c, i) => <>{i ? ", " : ""}<code>{c}</code></>)}. <code>verified=true</code> is a shortcut for <code>status=verified</code>.</li>
    <li><code>language</code>: <code>javascript</code> (published on npm) or <code>python</code> (published on PyPI). Tools without a package (hosted APIs, skills, source-only servers) have no language.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Example response</h3>
  <pre><code>{sample}</code></pre>
  <h3>Errors</h3>
  <p>Errors use the HTTP status and a JSON body: <code>{`{"error": {"status": 404, "code": "not_found", "message": "…"}}`}</code>. Codes: <code>invalid_parameter</code> (400, with the allowed values), <code>not_found</code> (404), <code>method_not_allowed</code> (405), <code>rate_limited</code> (429).</p>
  <h3 id="limits">Rate limits</h3>
  <p>No key and no sign-up. Fair use is about {RATE_LIMITS.api} requests per minute per IP for the REST API and {RATE_LIMITS.mcp} per minute for the MCP server. Limits are counted per Cloudflare edge instance, so treat them as a ceiling, not a quota. Every response has <code>RateLimit-Limit</code>, <code>RateLimit-Remaining</code> and <code>RateLimit-Reset</code> headers. Over the limit you get <code>429</code> with <code>Retry-After</code> (seconds). If you need everything, download <code>/api/v1/tools.json</code> once and cache it: the data changes about once a week.</p>

  <h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
  <h3>curl</h3>
  <pre><code>{curl}</code></pre>
  <h3>JavaScript (fetch)</h3>
  <pre><code>{js}</code></pre>
  <h3>Python (requests)</h3>
  <pre><code>{py}</code></pre>
  <h3>Prompt for an LLM agent with web access</h3>
  <pre><code>{prompt}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="mcp">Remote MCP server</h2>
  <p>The same data as an MCP server for Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor and other AI clients. URL: <code>{MCP_URL}</code>. Transport: Streamable HTTP (JSON responses, stateless, no sign-in). Protocol versions: {MCP_VERSIONS.map((v, i) => <>{i ? ", " : ""}<code>{v}</code></>)}.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {MCP_TOOLS.map((t) => <tr><td><code>{t.name}({Object.keys(t.inputSchema.properties).map((k) => (t.inputSchema.required ?? []).includes(k) ? k : `${k}?`).join(", ")})</code></td><td>{t.description}</td></tr>)}
  </tbody></table></div>
  <p>All three tools are read-only. The same rate limit, CORS and data rules apply as for the REST API.</p>
  <h3>Claude (desktop or web): custom connector</h3>
  <p>Claude → Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector, name it TradingAIHub and paste <code>{MCP_URL}</code>. No authentication is needed.</p>
  <h3>Claude Desktop: config file (mcp-remote)</h3>
  <p>If custom connectors aren't available on your plan, add this to <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code> (needs Node.js) and restart Claude:</p>
  <pre><code>{claudeDesktop}</code></pre>
  <h3>Claude Code</h3>
  <pre><code>{`claude mcp add --transport http tradingaihub ${MCP_URL}`}</code></pre>
  <h3>Cursor</h3>
  <p>Add to <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code> (project) or <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code> (global):</p>
  <pre><code>{cursor}</code></pre>
  <h3>VS Code (GitHub Copilot)</h3>
  <p>Add to <code>.vscode/mcp.json</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>{vscode}</code></pre>
  <h3>ChatGPT</h3>
  <p>ChatGPT → Settings → Apps &amp; Connectors → Advanced settings → turn on developer mode, then Create: name TradingAIHub, MCP server URL <code>{MCP_URL}</code>, authentication: none.</p>
  <h3>Raw JSON-RPC</h3>
  <pre><code>{rpc}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="licence">Licence</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Data</b> (API responses, MCP results and the JSON dumps): <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>. You may copy, adapt and use it, including commercially, if you credit <b>“TradingAIHub, https://tradingaihub.com”</b> (a link back is enough) and indicate changes. Every response carries <code>license</code>, <code>license_url</code> and <code>attribution</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Code</b>: MIT (API and MCP server code). The scope and exact files are listed in <a href="https://github.com/skyboundropship-code/tradingaihub/blob/main/LICENSE-CODE" rel="license noopener"><code>LICENSE-CODE</code></a>; the rest of the site's code and content is not licensed for reuse. The API index returns this as <code>code_license</code>.</li>
    <li>Tool names and trademarks belong to their owners.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="discovery">Discovery</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/api/openapi.json">/api/openapi.json</a>: OpenAPI 3.1 spec of the REST API.</li>
    <li><code>/mcp/server-card</code>: MCP Server Card (name, endpoint, protocol versions), and <code>/.well-known/ai-catalog.json</code>, which points to it.</li>
    <li><a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> and <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a>: the directory as plain text for LLMs.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Questions or a bug? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}?subject=API`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
</div>
</Base>
